Debug validation (post_balance_non_root_validation, lines 3973-4210) provides empirical verification:

1. The validation iterates through all output pages sequentially (lines 4016-4088)
2. For each cell in each output page, it checks:
   - cells_debug[current_index_cell] == cell_buf (the cell in the output page)
3. current_index_cell increments by exactly 1 for each cell found
4. If any cell were duplicated, the sequential index would advance incorrectly and the comparison would fail

Code (lines 4025-4038):
```rust
for cell_idx in 0..contents.cell_count() {
    // ... get cell_buf from page
    let cell_buf_in_array = &cells_debug[current_index_cell];
    if cell_buf != cell_buf_in_array {
        tracing::error!("balance_non_root(cell_not_found_debug, ...)");
        valid = false;
    }
    current_index_cell += 1;
}
```

This sequential check ensures a 1:1 correspondence: each cell_array entry maps to exactly one output cell position.
